{
  "name": "Wendelstein",
  "_about": "THE WENDELSTEIN, the open stair tower of the late-Gothic Residenz (the Albrechtsburg's Grosser Wendelstein, 1471-1524; Torgau's after it): a 8-sided tower `R` to its corners standing out from a wing's front, a SPIRAL inside round an open eye (`eye`) from the door at its foot (the face toward +z) up to `H`, the floor it arrives at, in `turns` turns. Its fronts are nearly all opening: the foot an open arcade (`footH`), then 3 storeys of great `arch`-headed arches `winW` wide on piers `pier` wide, a balustrade band (`parapet`) under each; over `H` the loggia (`stageH`), a cornice, a GABLE (`gableH`) over every open face with PINNACLES at its corners, and the slate NEEDLE (`capRise`) with a finial. `climb` lifts each face's storeys by its share of a storey round the tower, so the openings climb with the stair (0: level, as at Meissen). The back faces are blind: set the tower so they stand in the wing's wall (its middle `a` = R cos(180/n) out from the wall's face, less `t`). Place it at its middle, yawed so +z faces out. Written by tools/archgen/late_gothic.py.",
